2	//! The checker path over a fixture project of hand-written cases (`tests/fixtures/cases`): the 14 of the checker-first
3	//! deep dive in `Cases.tsx`, and one component per further mapping rule in `Rules.tsx`. The answer is held to a JSON
4	//! snapshot made from a real `tsrs` (`tests/snapshots/`), three ways:
5	//!
6	//! - replayed from its recording (`cases.recording.json`), always: the converter's output over exactly the answers the
7	//!   real checker gave, with no binary;
8	//! - against a real `tsrs` (the built-in checker, or the binary `TSRS_BIN` names), which also holds the answer to be
9	//!   the same when the checker is asked last to first (type handles change with the order of queries; the answer may
10	//!   not);
11	//! - merged over the structural result, which puts a union's members back in the order they were written in.
12	//!
13	//! Refresh the recording and the snapshot with `cargo run -p caliper-docgen-semantic --example record_fixture --
14	//! $TSRS_BIN cases`, then `cargo insta review`.
